# OorjaMan design tokens

**Never hardcode brand colours.** Import from `@oorjaman/config`.

```ts
import { brandColors, colors } from "@oorjaman/config";
```

Canonical definitions: `packages/config/src/brand.ts` and `packages/config/src/colors.ts`.

---

# Brand wordmark colours (`brandColors`)

Use for **OorjaMan text lockups**, splash/welcome/auth headers, and green→blue loading accents.

| Token | Hex | Use |
|-------|-----|-----|
| `brandColors.oorja` | `#549048` | “Oorja” wordmark, green loading start |
| `brandColors.man` | `#1C4276` | “Man” wordmark, blue loading end |
| `brandColors.tagline` | `#9B9B9B` | `WE CLEAN. YOU GENERATE.` + gray loading label |
| `brandColors.gradientGreen` | `#549048` | Bar / gradient green endpoint |
| `brandColors.gradientBlue` | `#1C4276` | Bar / gradient blue endpoint |

**Wordmark rules**

- Split colours: `Oorja` → `oorja`, `Man` → `man` (never one flat colour).
- Tagline always `brandColors.tagline`, not oorja/man.
- Prefer `BrandWordmark` / `BrandLockup` components — not `logo-lockup-tagline.png` on white screens (JPEG white box).

**Man blue** — keep `#1C4276` range (readable navy). Do not revert to near-black (`#0B1C3A`, `#082B5B`).

---

# App semantic colours (`colors`)

Use for **buttons, surfaces, forms, navigation** — not split wordmark text.

| Token | Hex | Use |
|-------|-----|-----|
| `colors.primary` | `#1f8660` | Primary CTAs |
| `colors.foreground` | `#0f2938` | Body headings / structure |
| `colors.mutedForeground` | `#516a7b` | Secondary copy |
| `colors.background` | `#f6faf9` | Screen canvas |
| `colors.accent` | `#9fc93c` | Lime highlight (sparingly) |

---

# Forbidden

- Stale palette values (`#6FB53E`, `#0F4D92`, `#0B1C3A`, `#8BC53F`) in new UI
- Random hex / Tailwind colours outside tokens
- Neon, loud gradients, saturated reds/yellows unless explicitly requested

---

# UI quality

- Premium, spacious, clean hierarchy
- Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64
- Primary buttons: `colors.primary` bg, `colors.primaryForeground` text
- Typography: **Plus Jakarta Sans** in mobile apps (see `constants/fonts.ts`)
